From: TB520FU port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: tb520fu: drop DisplayPort audio link from sound card

The internal-display boot DTB disables the DisplayPort controller
(/soc@0/display-subsystem@ae00000/displayport-controller@af54000) so the
MSM component master can bind without an unavailable DP bridge. The
sound card still lists a "DisplayPort Playback" DAI link referencing
&mdss_dp0, which can never resolve on that DTB. qcom_snd_parse_of()
fails with "DisplayPort Playback: codec dai not found" and the card
stays in /sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred forever, even after WCD,
SoundWire and AW882xx links are bound.

Follow the SC8280XP Lenovo ThinkPad X13s precedent, which deletes
#sound-dai-cells from the unused eDP controller and omits any DP link
from its sound card. Drop the dp-playback-dai-link from the TB520FU
sound node; internal speakers (WCD + AW882xx via TDM), headset and
capture remain. USB-C DP audio can be re-added once the DP bridge is
enabled in a display configuration that actually provides it.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu-peripherals.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu-peripherals.dtsi
@@ -120,13 +120,6 @@
 			};
 		};
 
-		dp-playback-dai-link {
-			link-name = "DisplayPort Playback";
-			cpu { sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0>; };
-			codec { sound-dai = <&mdss_dp0>; };
-			platform { sound-dai = <&q6apm>; };
-		};
-
 		aw-spk-dai-link {
 			link-name = "AW882xx Playback";
 
